    "resource": "aws_iam_access_key.user",
    "issue": "IAM access key created for user",
    "risk": "Access keys are long-lived secrets that can be exfiltrated from state, CI/CD logs, developer environments, or outputs and then used for persistent unauthorized access.",
    "remediation": "Remove the aws_iam_access_key.user resource and use temporary credentials via an IAM role. If an access key is absolutely required, ensure secure rotation and do not expose it through outputs."
